The hard-link carry-forward costs about 300 µs per entry on this APFS volume, roughly the same as a full copy. Per-entry creation looks like the bottleneck, not bytes. I'll check whether a single recursive `clonefile` of a directory avoids the per-entry cost, and separate the per-file and per-byte components.
